bert French|Buses in County Mayo","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"GPSLatitude":{"value":"53.799125","source":"commons-desc-page"},"GPSLongitude":{"value":"-9.511394","source":"commons-desc-page"},"GPSMapDatum":{"value":"WGS-84","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"We've seen this vehicle IM 181 at <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/nlireland/6851004167/\"><b>Leenane before</b></a>, or at least its sister vehicle IM 180. It's supposed to be near Westport, Co. Mayo. Can any of you place this viaduct?\n<p>Can make out \"Percy A. Ha..., Secretary\" just behind the chap riding shotgun (who is, I'm fairly sure, wearing a silver Claddagh ring on the pinkie finger of his right hand).\n</p><p>What do these mean? To do with weight? Tyre pressure?\nU.W. 2-13-0-0\nF.A.W. 2-10-0-0\nB.A.W. 4-0-0-0\n</p><p>Date: After 1906 (Commercial Car factory opened at Luton)\n</p>\nNLI Ref.: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://catalogue.nli.ie/Record/vtls000316488\">L_ROY_11182</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"between 1906 and 1914<div style=\"display: none;\">date QS:P,+1950-00-00T00:00:00Z/7,P1319,+1906-00-00T00:00:00Z/9,P1326,+1914-00-00T00:00:00Z/9</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/nlireland/8571539286/\">https://www.flickr.com/photos/nlireland/8571539286/</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://catalogue.nli.ie/Record/vtls000316488\">L_ROY_11182</a> at the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.nli.ie/\">National Library of Ireland</a></li></ul>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"<bdi><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/en:Robert_French_(photographer)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:en:Robert French (photographer)\"><span title=\"Irish photographer, 1841-1917\">Robert French</span></a></bdi>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Permission":{"value":"No known copyright restrictions","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"No restrictions","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"No known copyright restrictions","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"LicenseUrl":{"value":"https://www.flickr.com/commons/usage/","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Copyrighted":{"value":"True","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}}}]},"61652550":{"pageid":61652550,"ns":6,"title":"File:Charabanc St Aubyn Street New Plymouth.jpg","imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":16139034,"width":10797,"height":8267,"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1d/Charabanc_St_Aubyn_Street_New_Plymouth.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charabanc_St_Aubyn_Street_New_Plymouth.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=61652550","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2017-08-13 11:06:26","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"Charabanc St Aubyn Street New Plymouth","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"Large images|PD-New Zealand|White Motor Company buses|PD-old missing SDC copyright status|Motorized charabancs|Transport in New Plymouth|Buses in New Plymouth","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_Motor_Company\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:White Motor Company\">White Motor Company</a> Charabanc circa 1920 with B F Goodrich tyres in St Aubyn Street, New Plymouth","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"1930-01-01","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://collections.tepapa.govt.nz/Object/123419\">Te Papa Tongarewa</a> Museum of New Zealand","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"<p>Production\tOakley, William, circa 1930 <br>\n</p>\nF B Butler/Crown Studios Collection. Gift of Frederick B Butler, 1971","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}}}]},"24252318":{"pageid":24252318,"ns":6,"title":"File:Cherry Bounce (6851004167).jpg","imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":671212,"width":2451,"height":1890,"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/00/Cherry_Bounce_%286851004167%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cherry_Bounce_(6851004167).jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=24252318","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2013-01-27 07:59:30","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"Cherry Bounce (6851004167)","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"Ireland in the 1900s|History of tourism in Ireland|Sightseeing buses in Ireland|Leenaun|History of County Galway|Hotels in County Galway|Flickr images reviewed by File Upload Bot (Magnus Manske)|Images from the National Library of Ireland|Files from Flickr's 'The Commons'|1900s buses|Buses photographed in the 1900s|Files with coordinates missing SDC location of creation|Motorized charabancs|Vintage luggage and traveling equipment|Buses in County Galway","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"GPSLatitude":{"value":"53.595821","source":"commons-desc-page"},"GPSLongitude":{"value":"-9.696629","source":"commons-desc-page"},"GPSMapDatum":{"value":"WGS-84","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"<p>Completely stealing the title for this one from <i>Little Women</i> where Amy uses the term that the March family's household helper, Hannah, used for Mr. Laurence's Char-a-Banc.\n</p><p>This gorgeous touring car is pictured outside a hotel at Leenane (sometimes aka Leenaun), Co. Galway. From other photos in this sequence, the reg. no. of this vehicle is either IM 180 or 181. The touring car was provided by Commercial Cars in Luton, and the tour itself was in conjunction with the Midland Great Western Railway of Ireland Company, and the route was Clifden-Westport.\n</p><p>Said this morning that if anyone could identify the hotel, it would make an old Library very happy... <b><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/gnmcauley/\">Niall McAuley</a></b> did just that with his identification of this hotel as the Leenane Hotel!\n</p><p>Date: Circa 1907\n</p>\nNLI Ref.: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://catalogue.nli.ie/Record/L_ROY_06768\">L_ROY_06768</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"1907","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/nlireland/6851004167/\">Cherry Bounce</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/people/47290943@N03\">National Lib